From dfaebe5eddaea225a247334f3e56212bf476f69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:16:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: RT-N18U: add port 5 for the flow
 accelerator traps

Describe switch port 5, connected to gmac0, as a second CPU port with a
fixed link. b53 redirects the frames that the flow accelerator in front
of port 8 cannot handle (TTL 0 and 1, TCP FIN and RST) to it. The switch
boots with the regular tag; the bcm53xx preinit hook moves it to the
prepended tag when flow offloading and hardware flow offloading are both
on. User ports keep port 8 as their CPU port. This RT-N18U's switch
reports revision 5 at boot ("found switch: BCM53011, rev 5"), which has
the accelerator.

Measured on an RT-N18U: with hardware flow offloading off the switch
kept the regular tag and the accelerator stayed out of the path; with
both options on the hook moved it to the prepended tag at boot and a
TCP stream ran through the accelerator at 949 Mbit/s.

Signed-off-by: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts
@@ -134,7 +134,10 @@
 		};
 
 		port@5 {
-			status = "disabled";
+			fixed-link {
+				speed = <1000>;
+				full-duplex;
+			};
 		};
 
 		port@7 {
